#imputate vcf file using BEAGLE

WARNING! When filtering the raw datafile, in the recoding steps, for some loci in few individuals the missing alleles are are recoded as "." and not "./." (should be related to the use of --maf filtering with vcftools)

THIS RECODING causes few errors in beagle, which asks to remove these target loci
 
SO after checking on the internet (Biostars site) I've found a perl command which I slightly modified to use it with macox:

cat /gatk/data/Cece/EMCAP_533/EMCAP_532_SNPs_chr1-8_miss90.vcf.recode.vcf | perl -pe "s/\s\.:/\t.\/.:/g" > /gatk/data/Cece/EMCAP_533/EMCAP_532_SNPs_chr1-8_miss90_ready_beagle.vcf.recode.vcf


java -Xmx50g -jar beagle.28Jun21.220.jar gt=/gatk/data/Cece/EMCAP_533/EMCAP_532_SNPs_chr1-8_miss90_ready_beagle.vcf.recode.vcf out=/gatk/data/Cece/EMCAP_533/EMCAP_532_SNPs_chr1-8_miss90_imputated.vcf

# filter il file 208 accession

vcftools --gzvcf /gatk/data/Cece/EMCAP_533/EMCAP_532_SNPs_chr1-8_miss90_imputated.vcf.vcf.gz --keep genolist_geolocalized.txt  --recode --recode-INFO-all --out /gatk/data/Cece/EMCAP_533/EMCAP_208_geolocalize_miss90.vcf 

# to reduce the number of SNP lets tray to do a thinning of 50Kb
vcftools --vcf /gatk/data/Cece/EMCAP_533/EMCAP_208_geolocalize_miss90.vcf.recode.vcf --thin 10000  --recode --recode-INFO-all --out /gatk/data/Cece/EMCAP_533/EMCAP_533_SNPs_chr1-8_geolocalize_miss90_thinned10Kb.vcf
